template:media_split.contracts:
web/js/dynamic/templates/media_split.js

Default export: a TemplateModule `{id: 'media_split', build, layout, update, focusRect, itemEl, dimGroups, anchor, mediaBox, tex, texts}`.

Hooks:
- `focusRect(ctx, target)`:
  - `panel` gives the frame (shape rect, radius 24), only once the medium is visible;
  - `panel:row:<n>` gives terminal output line n (shape bar), null without it;
  - `<item>` gives the item's row (radius 8) while its alpha > 0.01;
  - every result is on whole px and carries `el`.
- `itemEl(ctx, id)`: the item's rich fields (`.dyn-ms-field`), one element, or `[term, text]` for a definition. Null for an unknown id or `option:<i>`.
- `dimGroups`: `[titleGroup?, ...itemGroups, mediaGroup]`.
- `mediaBox(scene, zones, mode, slot, fixes)`: pushHeadroom of the largest shown box. 16:9 gives {w: 995, h: 910}. 9:16 depends on the scene (title, items, pushes). The same for every slot and every fix.
- `tex(scene)`: `texOf(scene)`.
- `texts`: these entries:

| Slot | Role | Critical | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `title` | title | yes | weight 700 |
| `body` | body | yes | weight 400 in 16:9 (700 for heading/takeaway); 700 in 9:16 |
| `terminal` | body | yes | mono; on surface |
| (none) | label | no | the missing-medium label |

Exported pure helpers and constants (tested):
- Data: `ID`, `LABELS`, `TEXT_KINDS` (pinned equal to templates.py TEXT_KINDS), `VARIANTS`, `DEFAULT_VARIANT` ('media_right').
- `LAYOUT`:
  - landscape: title {max 88, min 64, lines 3, lh 1.08}; body {max 52, min 44, lh 1.3}; bodyWeight 400; gutter 24; marker 36; dot 14; titleGap 40; itemGap 24; terminal {max 44, min 36, lh 1.35, weight 400, pad 32};
  - portrait: title {max 88, min 56, lines 2, prefer 1, lh 1.06}; body {max 64, min 48, lines 2, lh 1.2}; bodyWeight 700; stageGap 24; phraseBottom 1032; terminal {max 44, min 40, lh 1.35, weight 700, pad 28}.
- Motion and type constants: `TITLE_WEIGHT`, `TITLE_TRACKING_EM`, `MISSING_LABEL_PX`, `TITLE_DELAY` 0.08, `TEXT_ENTER` 0.45, `MEDIA_ENTER` 0.5, `MEDIA_FROM` 0.96, `MEDIA_DELAY` 0.15, `EXIT_FACTOR` 0.7, `MIN_DWELL` 1.5.
- Functions:
  - `mediaOf(scene, mode)` → {slot, ref, start, shown};
  - `terminalOf(scene)`;
  - `textItemsOf(scene)`;
  - `variantOf(look)`;
  - `splitRegions(variant)` → {media, text};
  - `pushArea(zone, origins, scale?)`;
  - `pushTargets(scene)` → {item, panel};
  - `portraitBoxes(scene, titleH, phraseH)` → {title, phrase, media};
  - `phraseSchedule(timings, duration, scale?)`;
  - `landscapeColumn(text, zone, frame, push, panelOrigin, centres)`;
  - `texOf(scene)`.
- CSS classes the template sets (all styling is inline; no dynamic.css change needed): `dyn-ms`, `dyn-ms--<format>`, `dyn-ms-title`, `dyn-ms-column`, `dyn-ms-item`, `dyn-ms-text`, `dyn-ms-field`, `dyn-ms-label`, `dyn-ms-dot`, `dyn-ms-marker`, `dyn-ms-exit`, `dyn-ms-frame`, `dyn-ms-missing`, `dyn-ms-term`, `dyn-ms-term-cmd`, `dyn-ms-term-line`, `dyn-ms-scrim`; plus the shared `dyn-group` and `dyn-reveal-mask`.

Fixture generator: `python -m tests.compose.dynamic.make_media_split_fixtures [--check]` (byte-deterministic: sorted keys, two-space indent, LF).

